"How am l going to feed the children? "

947
01:14:03.360 --> 01:14:05.669
How can I afford it?

948
01:14:10.680 --> 01:14:16.152
We found this couple
living and freezing in the shanty town

949
01:14:16.200 --> 01:14:18.794
They're homeless
and have a week-old baby

950
01:14:19.760 --> 01:14:24.356
(Woman) What's it like
to live in these conditions?

951
01:14:24.400 --> 01:14:32.557
The cold at night is hardest for the baby,

952
01:14:32.600 --> 01:14:35.433
Do many people live like this in Chile?

953
01:14:35.480 --> 01:14:46.709
There are plenty, and worse off than we are,
They don't get any help from anyone,

954
01:14:46.760 --> 01:14:48.318
Where will you go?

955
01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:54.196
Back to the streets,
We've slept rough before,

956
01:14:55.560 --> 01:15:06.630
Abroad, in Europe and the USA, it's said that
life in Chile is rich and comfortable - is that so?

957
01:15:06.680 --> 01:15:12.152
It's true for the well off, but not for us,

958
01:15:13.560 --> 01:15:16.916
Chile is a democracy now, in theory

959
01:15:16.960 --> 01:15:23.149
A complicated voting system splits the vote
and discourages real reform

960
01:15:23.200 --> 01:15:26.192
It's a product of General Pinochet

961
01:15:26.240 --> 01:15:31.268
based on a constitution
that's also a product of Pinochet

962
01:15:32.120 --> 01:15:36.591
The general may be dead
but the power of the military remains

963
01:15:38.360 --> 01:15:43.992
It's all very modern the media is safe
and many believe it's wise to be silent

964
01:15:44.040 --> 01:15:47.430
Like the graves of their forgotten compatriots

965
01:15:48.360 --> 01:15:51.875
It's Washington’s ideal democracy

966
01:15:53.760 --> 01:15:59.551
The dictatorship was a great success in Chile
in that it established

967
01:15:59.600 --> 01:16:05.675
the political, economic and social model
that prevails to this day,

968
01:16:05.720 --> 01:16:12.910
Basically, the constitution imposed in 1 980
has not been changed,

969
01:16:12.960 --> 01:16:18.353
We don't belong to a democracy
because that word has been so badly used,

970
01:16:18.400 --> 01:16:20.118
It's not understood,

971
01:16:20.160 --> 01:16:25.678
Here there is a persecution against the poor,
and not just in Chile,

972
01:16:25.720 --> 01:16:28.553
but this is happening all over Latin America,

973
01:16:28.600 --> 01:16:40.478
I think. educated people realize
that this is reaching a breaking point,

974
01:16:41.400 --> 01:16:45.916
I believe the people will wake up
and say, "That's enough,"

975
01:16:55.640 --> 01:16:57.039
This is Bolivia

976
01:16:57.080 --> 01:16:59.355
another laboratory experiment

977
01:17:00.640 --> 01:17:06.636
The majority of the population of this spectacular
brutalized country high in the Andes

978
01:17:06.680 --> 01:17:09.752
have also been invisible until recently

979
01:17:17.040 --> 01:17:20.510
The indigenous people
the Aymara and Quechua

980
01:17:20.560 --> 01:17:24.951
carry memories of a culture
and civilization and wealth

981
01:17:25.000 --> 01:17:28.959
Iong before the Spanish arrived
5000years ago

982
01:17:30.040 --> 01:17:35.034
They remember how a single hill of silver
underwrote the entire Spanish empire

983
01:17:35.080 --> 01:17:37.469
while they became the poorest

984
01:17:44.440 --> 01:17:46.749
This is the National Congress of Bolivia,

985
01:17:46.800 --> 01:17:50.509
Until recently,
the faces here were almost all white,

986
01:17:50.560 --> 01:17:55.588
the descendants of a tiny Spanish elite
which plundered the nation's riches

987
01:17:55.640 --> 01:17:59.599
and reduced the indigenous majority
to serfdom.

988
01:17:59.640 --> 01:18:03.349
It was a pattern of control
repeated all over Latin America,

989
01:18:03.400 --> 01:18:05.789
The pattern has been broken in Bolivia

990
01:18:05.840 --> 01:18:11.039
with the rise of social justice movements
of a kind never seen before,

991
01:18:11.080 --> 01:18:15.710
and whose democratic home
is not Westminster or Washington,

992
01:18:15.760 --> 01:18:17.716
or any other so-called model,

993
01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:23.392
but in the streets, the minds,
the barrios, the fields,

994
01:18:23.440 --> 01:18:28.195
Governments that defy this popular power,
this true democracy,

995
01:18:28.240 --> 01:18:30.595
do so at their own peril,

996
01:18:36.920 --> 01:18:42.153
This is El Alto the highest city on earth
and perhaps the poorest

997
01:18:50.760 --> 01:18:55.151
The occupants of this cemetery
on the roof of the world are mainly children

998
01:18:58.200 --> 01:19:02.273
Protected they say
by the sacred mountain, Illimani

999
01:19:02.320 --> 01:19:05.517
El Alto overlooks Bolivia 's capital La Paz

1000
01:19:13.640 --> 01:19:19.670
Juan Delfin, a priest and a taxi driver
has lived here for most of his life

1001
01:19:22.560 --> 01:19:30.069
This is Villa lngenio,
It's the cemetery of northern El Alto,

1002
01:19:31.160 --> 01:19:35.551
There is a sorrowful bitterness here,

1003
01:19:35.600 --> 01:19:40.833
Our brothers, our children,
our grandparents

1004
01:19:40.880 --> 01:19:44.316
are dead and buried here,

1005
01:19:45.880 --> 01:19:48.997
There was one family
that poisoned themselves,

1006
01:19:49.040 --> 01:19:53.830
the whole family,
because of lack of work and lack of money,

1007
01:19:53.880 --> 01:19:58.078
First the husband poisoned his wife
and children, and then he poisoned himself,

1008
01:19:58.120 --> 01:19:59.599
We have seen cases like this,

1009
01:19:59.640 --> 01:20:01.232
(Car horns)

1010
01:20:03.520 --> 01:20:09.038
When I first came too Bolivia in the 1 960s
El Alto barely existed

1011
01:20:09.080 --> 01:20:13.198
The million people living here
are peasants run off their land

1012
01:20:13.240 --> 01:20:18.872
and miners made redundant by policies
similar to those imposed in Chile

1013
01:20:19.920 --> 01:20:24.436
Infrastructure that didn't make a quick buck
was privatized

1014
01:20:25.840 --> 01:20:27.592
The message was clear -

1015
01:20:27.640 --> 01:20:30.996
sell it, strip it or scrap it

1016
01:20:31.040 --> 01:20:34.032
The indigenous people were scrapped

1017
01:20:37.560 --> 01:20:39.630
(Juan Delfin) We wonder why,

1018
01:20:41.200 --> 01:20:47.673
If I am Bolivian, born rich,
why am l begging?

1019
01:20:47.720 --> 01:20:56.389
We had the sea, silver and gold,
We had everything, Why are we still suffering?

1020
01:20:59.920 --> 01:21:03.469
And yet the people here have held together

1021
01:21:03.520 --> 01:21:06.353
their sense of identity their community

1022
01:21:10.280 --> 01:21:11.793
(Singing)

1023
01:21:25.960 --> 01:21:30.954
In the year 200000, the people
of Bolivia’s second city Cochabamba

1024
01:21:31.000 --> 01:21:35.949
fought an epic struggle to win back
their most basic resource, water

1025
01:21:36.000 --> 01:21:42.030
from a foreign consortium dominated
by the American corporation Bechtel

1026
01:21:42.080 --> 01:21:44.071
and they won

1027
01:21:52.280 --> 01:21:55.192
Three years later, in 20003,

1028
01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:59.313
Bolivia 's power brokers
were about to get another shock.

1029
01:22:02.960 --> 01:22:06.748
This is Gonzalo Sanchez de Lozada

1030
01:22:06.800 --> 01:22:10.031
Known as Goni
he was brought up in Washington

1031
01:22:11.040 --> 01:22:12.951
His English is better than his Spanish

1032
01:22:14.200 --> 01:22:17.317
They knew him here as El Gringo

1033
01:22:18.920 --> 01:22:27.476
I saw him as a fat man
sitting on a golden chair,

1034
01:22:27.520 --> 01:22:29.795
Arrogant,

1035
01:22:29.840 --> 01:22:39.397
Perhaps he was arrogant because of
the power he had, which was his wealth,

1036
01:22:40.720 --> 01:22:45.271
When Goni was elected president of Bolivia
in 20003,

1037
01:22:45.320 --> 01:22:49.552
he backed a law that amounted too
a fire sale of the country’s resources

1038
01:22:51.480 --> 01:22:53.869
Almost everything was up for grabs

1039
01:22:53.920 --> 01:22:58.038
including Latin America's
second-biggest gas reserves

1040
01:22:58.080 --> 01:23:04.553
We know we have gas
and it's being sold abroad to the almighty US,

1041
01:23:04.600 --> 01:23:08.275
yet still I use wood for cooking,

1042
01:23:08.320 --> 01:23:10.436
This is why the war starts,

1043
01:23:10.480 --> 01:23:13.950
We will block, strike and demonstrate
until we get a response,

1044
01:23:16.640 --> 01:23:22.272
The people of El Alto fought back.
blocking the roads leading into La Paz

1045
01:23:28.920 --> 01:23:33.118
(Atencio) There were calls to start blockades,
Not even a fly would move,

1046
01:23:33.160 --> 01:23:44.071
We stopped traffic and so on, but it gradually,,,
What's the word?

1047
01:23:44.120 --> 01:23:46.111
It gradually intensified,

1048
01:23:50.320 --> 01:23:54.359
Gooni's response
was the traditional Latin American way

1049
01:23:55.160 --> 01:23:57.594
He sent in the army too crush dissent

1050
01:23:57.640 --> 01:23:59.198
(Shouting)

1051
01:23:59.240 --> 01:24:01.071
(Screaming)

1052
01:24:02.640 --> 01:24:04.631
Scores were shoot dead

1053
01:24:07.560 --> 01:24:08.959
(Gunfire)

1054
01:24:10.240 --> 01:24:14.597
Many were brought too Juan Delfin's church

1055
01:24:15.520 --> 01:24:24.679
The tables were here,
The bodies were here,

1056
01:24:27.720 --> 01:24:37.231
They removed the bullets with nails even,

1057
01:24:38.360 --> 01:24:41.670
It was sad to see this,

1058
01:24:50.560 --> 01:24:57.591
The place was full, There were doctors
everywhere, The smell of death was intense,

1059
01:25:02.040 --> 01:25:08.912
All the orphans were crying and shouting,
"Daddy! Daddy! Daddy!

1060
01:25:11.240 --> 01:25:14.869
Tens of thousands of people
poured down into La Paz

1061
01:25:16.800 --> 01:25:21.635
Like the people of Venezuela's barrios
demanding the return of their president

1062
01:25:21.680 --> 01:25:23.750
they demanded their country back.

1063
01:25:26.560 --> 01:25:29.996
If the rich and powerful of Latin America
had a nightmare

1064
01:25:30.040 --> 01:25:31.712
this was it

1065
01:25:33.560 --> 01:25:37.553
Suddenly we heard
that Goni was about to resign,

1066
01:25:37.600 --> 01:25:43.118
With one down, we felt inspired,
It gave us strength,

1067
01:25:43.160 --> 01:25:48.280
That was the aim. To make him resign,

1068
01:25:49.560 --> 01:25:51.790
Goni fled to the United States

1069
01:25:51.840 --> 01:25:55.310
and is today living in a smart suburb
of Washington

1070
01:25:56.120 --> 01:26:00.910
In October 20004
the Bolivian Congress ordered his arrest

1071
01:26:00.960 --> 01:26:03.997
on charges of bloody massacre

1072
01:26:04.040 --> 01:26:08.079
George Bush has said
"Governments that harbour terrorists

1073
01:26:08.120 --> 01:26:10.111
"are as guilty as they are"

1074
01:26:10.160 --> 01:26:12.674
(Speaking Spanish)

1075
01:26:15.720 --> 01:26:19.508
This extraordinary mural
was painted by Juan Delfin

1076
01:26:20.280 --> 01:26:24.398
It's a cry of freedom
from an entire continent

1077
01:26:24.440 --> 01:26:32.791
They killed us all, but we defend
the Aymara people with the pututo horn,

1078
01:26:32.840 --> 01:26:40.918
with our voice, with our fist, with the flag,

1079
01:26:40.960 --> 01:26:47.069
We wave the Whipala
against the United States,

1080
01:26:47.120 --> 01:26:52.478
This is the United States flag,
We are against this,

1081
01:26:52.520 --> 01:26:55.159
because they have put us
in the situation we are in,

1082
01:26:55.200 --> 01:26:57.589
The fist is very important,

1083
01:26:57.640 --> 01:27:02.998
That's how we are,
That's us,

1084
01:27:08.200 --> 01:27:12.910
In 20005 the people of Bolivia
took an historic step

1085
01:27:12.960 --> 01:27:19.877
For the first time ever, an indigenous person
was voted president in a landslide

1086
01:27:19.920 --> 01:27:22.388
Like Chavez in Venezuela

1087
01:27:22.440 --> 01:27:27.798
Evo Morales offered
a new democracy and a new beginning

1088
01:27:27.840 --> 01:27:34.996
We ask. everyone to start working,

1089
01:27:35.920 --> 01:27:37.990
The party is over,

1090
01:27:38.040 --> 01:27:41.635
The honeymoon is over,

1091
01:27:41.680 --> 01:27:44.274
And it's over forever, for a new Bolivia!

1092
01:27:46.360 --> 01:27:52.117
There is no doubt that it is growing,
It is propagating itself,

1093
01:27:52.160 --> 01:27:57.439
over the whole continent of Latin America,

1094
01:27:57.480 --> 01:28:01.075
of the Caribbean too,
but mainly in South America,

1095
01:28:01.120 --> 01:28:05.477
I go around Latin America

1096
01:28:05.520 --> 01:28:10.514
from Buenos Aires to Brasilia
and to Montevideo, La Paz,

1097
01:28:10.560 --> 01:28:14.155
There is a fervor sparking off everywhere,
There is a fervor,

1098
01:28:16.120 --> 01:28:21.353
In Latin America there's now a host of leaders
offering new beginnings

1099
01:28:21.400 --> 01:28:27.032
Of course, history is crowded with heroes
who offer new beginnings

1100
01:28:27.080 --> 01:28:34.191
The respectability of great power and its games
and deals and plunder always beckon

1101
01:28:35.320 --> 01:28:41.350
If these new leaders succumb their biggest
threat may not be from Washington

1102
01:28:41.400 --> 01:28:44.437
but from the people on the hillsides

1103
01:28:45.800 --> 01:28:50.112
# I was born by the river

1104
01:28:52.320 --> 01:28:54.117
#In a little tent

1105
01:28:54.960 --> 01:28:57.679
#Oh, and just like the river

1106
01:28:57.720 --> 01:29:02.714
#I been running ever since

1107
01:29:02.760 --> 01:29:06.036
#It’s been along

1108
01:29:06.920 --> 01:29:08.717
#A long time coming

1109
01:29:08.760 --> 01:29:13.959
# But I know a change gonna come

1110
01:29:15.400 --> 01:29:17.470
#Oh, yes, it will

1111
01:29:19.720 --> 01:29:22.917
#It's been too hard living

1112
01:29:23.880 --> 01:29:28.908
#But I'm afraid to die

1113
01:29:29.680 --> 01:29:33.673
# Cos I don't know what's up there

1114
01:29:33.720 --> 01:29:35.870
# Beyond the sky

1115
01:29:35.920 --> 01:29:39.515
#It's been a long

1116
01:29:40.360 --> 01:29:42.396
#A long time coming

1117
01:29:42.440 --> 01:29:45.477
#But l know

1118
01:29:45.520 --> 01:29:47.476
# A change gonna come

1119
01:29:48.440 --> 01:29:51.034
#Oh, yes, it will...

1120
01:29:51.080 --> 01:29:55.870
The future is for my children,
for our young people,

1121
01:29:55.920 --> 01:30:01.995
This isn't just Chavez's struggle,
it's our struggle,

1122
01:30:02.040 --> 01:30:06.511
What Chavez has unleashed
is a recognition of this struggle,

1123
01:30:06.560 --> 01:30:10.030
and we are in it together
and we'll carry on fighting,

1124
01:30:10.080 --> 01:30:13.516
So the empire's struggle isn't with Chavez,
it's with us,

1125
01:30:13.560 --> 01:30:16.074
The great awakening has arrived,

1126
01:30:16.120 --> 01:30:21.399
And I think Victor Hugo, let's end with him.
I'm with him on this,

1127
01:30:21.440 --> 01:30:30.758
Victor Hugo wrote this - "There is nothing
so powerful as an idea whose time has come,"

1128
01:30:31.680 --> 01:30:34.399
The American empire has reached its end

1129
01:30:34.440 --> 01:30:40.709
and the world must now be governed by
the rule of law, of equality, justice and fraternity,

1130
01:30:40.760 --> 01:30:44.469
Muchas gracias, John,
I want to see you again,

1131
01:30:47.920 --> 01:30:51.833
What happened here
at the National Stadium in Santiago, Chile,

1132
01:30:51.880 --> 01:30:55.873
has a special place in the struggle
for freedom and democracy

1133
01:30:55.920 --> 01:30:58.832
throughout Latin America and the world,

1134
01:30:58.880 --> 01:31:01.440
The vow is - never again,

1135
01:31:01.480 --> 01:31:05.155
And yet it has happened again
at Guantanamo Bay

1136
01:31:05.200 --> 01:31:07.111
and all the other secret places

1137
01:31:07.160 --> 01:31:11.836
where imperial power,
regardless of its democratic pretensions,

1138
01:31:11.880 --> 01:31:15.759
hides and tortures its perceived enemies,

1139
01:31:15.800 --> 01:31:19.190
The questions raised in this film are urgent,

1140
01:31:19.240 --> 01:31:23.119
Are the lives and dreams
of the ordinary people of Chile,

1141
01:31:23.160 --> 01:31:25.355
Like the people of Venezuela,

1142
01:31:25.400 --> 01:31:27.391
Like the people of Bolivia,

1143
01:31:27.440 --> 01:31:29.556
Like the people of Nicaragua,

1144
01:31:29.600 --> 01:31:31.636
Like the people of Vietnam,

1145
01:31:31.680 --> 01:31:35.229
and lraq, and lran, and Palestine,

1146
01:31:35.280 --> 01:31:40.593
expendable - worth only a few seconds
on the news if they're lucky?

1147
01:31:40.640 --> 01:31:44.030
The answer is no,
and those who see the world

1148
01:31:44.080 --> 01:31:47.516
through the eyes of the powerful,
should be warned,

1149
01:31:47.560 --> 01:31:50.916
People are rising
from the tyranny and oblivion

1150
01:31:50.960 --> 01:31:54.157
to which we in the West
have consigned them.

1151
01:31:54.200 --> 01:31:58.478
Indeed, their resistance is well under way
as this film has shown,

1152
01:31:58.520 --> 01:32:02.195
I would say it never stopped
and is unbeatable,

1153
01:32:05.560 --> 01:32:08.757
#I go to the movie

1154
01:32:09.680 --> 01:32:14.629
# And I go downtown

1155
01:32:15.840 --> 01:32:21.949
# Somebody keep telling me
don't hang around

1156
01:32:22.000 --> 01:32:25.197
#It’s been a long

1157
01:32:26.040 --> 01:32:28.031
#A long time coming

1158
01:32:28.080 --> 01:32:32.870
# But I know a change gonna come

1159
01:32:34.440 --> 01:32:36.396
#Oh, yes, it will

1160
01:32:40.880 --> 01:32:45.635
#Then I go to my brother

1161
01:32:49.120 --> 01:32:55.195
# And I say, "Brother, help me, please"

1162
01:32:57.720 --> 01:32:59.995
# But he winds up

1163
01:33:01.840 --> 01:33:03.876
#Knocking me

1164
01:33:05.840 --> 01:33:09.549
# Back. down on my knees

1165
01:33:09.600 --> 01:33:12.068
#Ohhh

1166
01:33:12.120 --> 01:33:21.233
# There been times that I thought
I couldn't last for long

1167
01:33:22.520 --> 01:33:28.595
# But now I think. I'm able to carry on

1168
01:33:28.640 --> 01:33:32.633
#It’s been a long

1169
01:33:32.680 --> 01:33:35.035
#Along time coming

1170
01:33:35.080 --> 01:33:37.150
#But l know

1171
01:33:37.960 --> 01:33:39.916
# A change gonna come

1172
